856
00:28:26.080 --> 00:28:26.320
Okay.
好吧。

857
00:28:26.440 --> 00:28:28.880
That seems to—I think that's kind of how polling is done, though.
不过我觉得，民意调查好像就是这么做的。

858
00:28:29.220 --> 00:28:30.300
Oh, let's not go there.
噢，我们还是别讨论这个了。

859
00:28:30.500 --> 00:28:30.780
Okay.
好吧。

860
00:28:31.260 --> 00:28:32.100
Well, I—
嗯，我——

861
00:28:32.100 --> 00:28:34.400
Charlie horse is just when your muscle seizes up.
“抽筋”（Charlie horse）只是指肌肉痉挛。

862
00:28:34.520 --> 00:28:38.780
I know that, but I kind of felt like it was like one of those things where Michael gets it a little wrong.
我知道，但我当时觉得这就像迈克尔又搞错的那种情况。

863
00:28:39.060 --> 00:28:42.760
Like, he's like, Charlie horse, but I was like, oh, did he mean how's a horse bite an apple?
就像他说“抽筋”，但我当时想，噢，他是不是想说马是怎么咬苹果的？

864
00:28:42.760 --> 00:28:48.120
But probably not, because that's too many words, and he had to cross the whole room really quickly.
但可能不是，因为那话太长了，而且他当时必须很快地穿过整个房间。

865
00:28:50.120 --> 00:28:55.680
Well, Michael also gets Dwight to go over to accounting and dump their stuff all over the ground.
嗯，迈克尔还让德怀特去会计部，把他们的东西全扔在地上。

866
00:28:56.200 --> 00:28:58.720
We had a fan question from Alan3.
我们收到了一个来自Alan3的粉丝提问。

867
00:28:59.100 --> 00:29:02.200
How many times did Stephen Rayne mess up the accounting area?
史蒂夫和雷恩一共搞乱了会计部多少次？

868
00:29:02.400 --> 00:29:03.900
Did they do it randomly, or was it choreographed?
他们是随机做的，还是排练好的？

869
00:29:04.420 --> 00:29:06.060
Angela, can you give us some insight?
安吉拉，你能给我们透露一下吗？

870
00:29:06.280 --> 00:29:07.620
We did it a few times.
我们拍了好几次。

871
00:29:07.620 --> 00:29:14.280
And, you know, so every time Michael would say, okay, let's send up accounting, old-fashioned raid, sales on accounting, they would come over.
你知道的，每次迈克尔说“好了，去会计部突袭一下，老派作风，销售部去会计部”，他们就会过来。

872
00:29:14.560 --> 00:29:15.980
They'd dump all of our stuff on the floor.
他们会把我们所有的东西都扔到地板上。

873
00:29:16.240 --> 00:29:19.260
I did love that Angela glares at Dwight, like, don't even.
我确实很喜欢安吉拉瞪德怀特的那种眼神，好像在说“你敢”。

874
00:29:19.620 --> 00:29:24.280
And so he sort of giggles and picks up one pencil and throws it on the floor of mine.
然后他就会咯咯笑，捡起一支铅笔扔在我的地板上。

875
00:29:24.560 --> 00:29:32.280
But, yeah, we did that a few times, and they were just—really, truly just looked like Steve and Rayne were having fun, because they got to come over and mess with us.
但是，是的，我们拍了好几次，他们真的、真的看起来就像史蒂夫和雷恩玩得很开心，因为他们终于可以过来找我们麻烦了。

876
00:29:32.280 --> 00:29:40.520
And then, so after you shoot a scene like that, and they mess up the area, they say cut, did the set decorators come over and reset everything?
那么，在拍完这样的场景，他们把区域弄乱之后，导演喊停，布景师会过来重置一切吗？

877
00:29:40.800 --> 00:29:43.520
They do, because they want the continuity to match.
他们会的，因为他们想保持连贯性。

878
00:29:43.620 --> 00:29:43.820
Yeah.
是的。

879
00:29:44.220 --> 00:29:48.800
And, you know, obviously we would pick up stuff as well, but sometimes we would get in the way.
而且，你知道，显然我们也会捡东西，但有时我们会碍事。

880
00:29:48.940 --> 00:29:51.280
Like, we would start to pick it up, and they'd be like, here, let me set that.
比如，我们刚开始捡，他们就会说，来，让我来摆放。

881
00:29:51.440 --> 00:29:56.800
Because that is their job, to make sure it looks exactly like it did before, and I might not get it right.
因为那是他们的工作，要确保一切看起来和之前一模一样，而我可能弄不对。

882
00:29:56.800 --> 00:30:03.740
So I remember sometimes before scenes like this, our script supervisor, Veda, she is the person who was in charge of continuity on the show.
所以我记得有时在这样的场景之前，我们的场记维达（Veda），就是负责剧中连贯性的人。

883
00:30:04.140 --> 00:30:09.940
She would come over and take a picture of the desk area as a reference point.
她会过来给办公桌区域拍张照作为参考点。

884
00:30:10.120 --> 00:30:11.680
So they could match it each time.
这样他们每次都能对上。

885
00:30:11.820 --> 00:30:18.820
Yes, and then after it got all messed up, then Veda would come over with her computer, and she'd be like, okay, so this is exactly where the cup was, and this is where this was,
是的，然后在一切被弄乱之后，维达会带着她的电脑过来，她会说，好了，杯子原本就在这里，这个东西在这里，

886
00:30:18.820 --> 00:30:19.280
and everything.
还有其他所有东西。

887
00:30:19.400 --> 00:30:23.360
And they would reset the whole thing to Veda's picture and then mess it up again.
他们会按照维达的照片重置整个场景，然后再把它弄乱。

888
00:30:23.360 --> 00:30:32.680
Yes, Veda was amazing, and she was so sweet and kind and soft-spoken, and sometimes she would just walk up to you and be like, Angela, on the second line in the scene,
是的，维达太棒了，她非常甜美、善良、说话轻声细语，有时她会直接走到你面前说，安吉拉，在这一场的第二句台词里，

889
00:30:32.840 --> 00:30:36.040
you switched your coffee mug from your left hand to your right hand.
你把咖啡杯从左手换到了右手。

890
00:30:36.860 --> 00:30:38.340
I'd be like, oh, my God, did I?
我会说，天哪，我有吗？

891
00:30:38.380 --> 00:30:39.160
I didn't even realize.
我甚至都没意识到。

892
00:30:39.340 --> 00:30:41.220
Yes, so you have to do that every time now.
是的，所以你现在每次都必须那样做。

893
00:30:42.200 --> 00:30:43.760
Yes, I remember that.
是的，我记得那个。

894
00:30:44.240 --> 00:30:45.180
I remember that.
我记得那个。

895
00:30:45.340 --> 00:30:50.580
At 8 minutes, 55 seconds, I'm calling this the fan catch of the day.
在8分55秒处，我称之为今日最佳粉丝发现。

896
00:30:50.800 --> 00:30:51.520
What is it?
是什么？

897
00:30:51.520 --> 00:30:52.860
It is by Biro.
是Biro发现的。

898
00:30:53.540 --> 00:31:07.100
If you freeze and zoom in on Angela's computer, you can see a Post-it note that says, quote, Angela, can I have $5 petty cash to buy some more jelly beans?
如果你暂停并放大安吉拉的电脑，你可以看到一张便利贴，上面写着：“安吉拉，我能拿5美元零用钱去买些软糖吗？

899
00:31:07.300 --> 00:31:08.960
I'll give you back any change.
剩下的钱我会还给你的。

900
00:31:09.160 --> 00:31:09.900
Thanks, Pam.
谢谢，帕姆。”

901
00:31:11.060 --> 00:31:12.380
Catch of the day.
今日特供。

902
00:31:12.380 --> 00:31:13.360
That is fantastic.
那太棒了。

903
00:31:13.360 --> 00:31:14.460
I loved that.
我喜欢那个。

904
00:31:14.960 --> 00:31:17.200
I think I really wrote that Post-it note.
我觉得那张便利贴真的是我写的。

905
00:31:17.360 --> 00:31:18.100
You probably did.
你可能确实写过。

906
00:31:18.100 --> 00:31:21.820
You probably passed it to me in the background because we were bored, and I stuck it there.
可能当时我们太无聊了，你把它递给我，我就贴在那儿了。

907
00:31:22.720 --> 00:31:30.260
So then Michael has a talking head about former manager Ed Truck, and this has one of my favorite Michael quotes.
接下来迈克尔有一段关于前经理埃德·塔克的采访，里面有我最喜欢的迈克尔语录之一。

908
00:31:30.260 --> 00:31:37.040
I told myself if I was ever manager, people would laugh when they saw me coming and applaud when I walked away.
我告诉自己，如果我当上经理，人们看到我走来时会发笑，而我离开时他们会鼓掌。

909
00:31:38.040 --> 00:31:38.920
Mission accomplished.
任务达成。

910
00:31:39.100 --> 00:31:39.880
Yeah, way to go.
没错，干得漂亮。

911
00:31:40.080 --> 00:31:42.580
I just want to call out one scene, you guys.
伙计们，我想特别提一下一个场景。

912
00:31:42.780 --> 00:31:45.620
I know we're jumping around a little, but it's one I absolutely love.
我知道我们跳跃得有点多，但这一个我绝对超爱。

913
00:31:45.680 --> 00:31:51.580
At 9 minutes, 55 seconds, it made me laugh so hard when Dwight is trying to be the 107th caller.
在9分55秒的时候，德怀特试图成为第107位打进电话的人，那段真的让我笑得不行。

914
00:31:51.820 --> 00:31:52.220
Yes!
没错！

915
00:31:52.220 --> 00:31:54.600
To win a DVD box set.
为了赢一套DVD礼盒。

916
00:31:54.740 --> 00:31:55.860
Of Jethro Tull.
杰叟罗·塔乐团的。

917
00:31:56.480 --> 00:31:57.000
Yes!
对！

918
00:31:57.160 --> 00:31:58.200
From Rock 107.
来自107摇滚电台。

919
00:31:58.500 --> 00:32:05.840
And he just keeps calling, and Michael's pained expression, and then Dwight trying to sneak the call, just all of it just cracked me up.
他不停地打，迈克尔那痛苦的表情，还有德怀特试图偷偷打电话的样子，这一切都让我笑喷了。

920
00:32:06.000 --> 00:32:12.740
One of the fun dynamics about the Michael and Dwight relationship is that it gives Steve an opportunity to play the straight man.
迈克尔和德怀特关系中一个有趣的动态是，它给了史蒂夫扮演“捧哏”的机会。

921
00:32:13.000 --> 00:32:13.180
Yeah.
没错。

922
00:32:13.180 --> 00:32:20.260
And he's a very funny straight man, and so a lot of times he's the funny guy, and the rest of us are the straight man to Steve,
他是个非常有趣的“捧哏”，因为很多时候他是那个搞笑的人，而我们其他人则是史蒂夫的“捧哏”。

923
00:32:20.440 --> 00:32:24.380
but I love this dynamic shift that happens with Michael and Dwight scenes.
但我很喜欢迈克尔和德怀特场景中出现的这种动态转换。

924
00:32:24.500 --> 00:32:24.980
I do too.
我也喜欢。

925
00:32:25.200 --> 00:32:28.380
I want you to know I did a little bit of a deep dive for Rock 107.
我想让你知道，我为了107摇滚电台做了一点深入调查。

926
00:32:28.640 --> 00:32:29.780
I knew you would.
我就知道你会这么做。

927
00:32:29.780 --> 00:32:32.240
I almost did, but you know what I did instead?
我本来也想做，但你知道我后来做了什么吗？

928
00:32:32.480 --> 00:32:32.660
What?
什么？

929
00:32:32.820 --> 00:32:34.200
I listened to Jethro Tull.
我听了杰叟罗·塔乐团的歌。

930
00:32:34.520 --> 00:32:34.780
Oh!
噢！

931
00:32:35.440 --> 00:32:36.300
There you go.
这就对了。

932
00:32:36.300 --> 00:32:41.300
I downloaded the greatest hits and listened to it, and my daughter Isabel was like, what is that?
我下载了他们的精选集听了听，我女儿伊莎贝尔问我，那是什么？

933
00:32:42.060 --> 00:32:53.460
Well, they currently run contests via their Freeloaders Club, and you can sign up with your email at rock107.com, and they give away, quote, dozens of prizes each month.
嗯，他们目前通过“免费客俱乐部”举办比赛，你可以在rock107.com用邮箱注册，他们每个月会送出，引用一下，几十个奖品。

934
00:32:53.640 --> 00:32:55.520
Here's a list of things you can win.
这是你可以赢取的奖品清单。

935
00:32:55.640 --> 00:32:55.880
Okay.
好的。

936
00:32:56.340 --> 00:33:04.140
iPads, water park tickets, concert tickets, gas and grocery gifts, and snow tube passes, maybe for the Poconos?
iPad、水上乐园门票、演唱会门票、加油和超市购物卡，还有雪圈票，可能是波科诺山的？

937
00:33:04.460 --> 00:33:04.880
Maybe.
也许吧。

938
00:33:05.060 --> 00:33:06.320
Those are great gifts, though.
不过那些都是很棒的礼物。

939
00:33:06.480 --> 00:33:06.840
I know.
我知道。

940
00:33:06.940 --> 00:33:08.380
Way to go, Rock 107.
干得好，107摇滚电台。

941
00:33:08.380 --> 00:33:15.760
It seems like instead of doing these live contests on the air where you have to call in like Dwight did, you can just sign up with your email, and you're automatically entered.
看起来与其像德怀特那样在直播中进行必须打电话进来的比赛，你只需要用邮箱注册，就能自动参与。

942
00:33:16.000 --> 00:33:19.540
So just giving a plug for that giveaway, Rock 107.
所以就给那个抽奖活动打个广告吧，107摇滚电台。

943
00:33:19.780 --> 00:33:20.360
Way to go.
干得好。

944
00:33:20.640 --> 00:33:22.900
I have 10 minutes, 44 seconds.
我这边是10分44秒。

945
00:33:23.340 --> 00:33:23.600
Okay.
好的。

946
00:33:23.840 --> 00:33:27.800
Pam and Roy are flirting at reception, and Jim is watching her in the kitchen.
帕姆和罗伊在前台调情，吉姆在厨房看着她。

947
00:33:27.800 --> 00:33:30.400
He tries to go to the annex, but he sees Kelly.
他想去附楼，但他看到了凯莉。

948
00:33:31.020 --> 00:33:32.360
Then he goes to the bathroom.
然后他去了洗手间。

949
00:33:32.600 --> 00:33:33.840
With his coffee mug.
带着他的咖啡杯。

950
00:33:34.020 --> 00:33:34.180
Yeah.
没错。

951
00:33:34.180 --> 00:33:35.380
This is how trapped he is.
他就是这样被困住了。

952
00:33:35.380 --> 00:33:36.940
One way, it's Pam and Roy.
一边是帕姆和罗伊。

953
00:33:37.060 --> 00:33:38.000
The other way, it's Kelly.
另一边是凯莉。

954
00:33:38.140 --> 00:33:39.080
Chatty, chatty, chatty.
喋喋不休，没完没了。

955
00:33:39.180 --> 00:33:41.720
So he just walks in the bathroom with his coffee mug.
所以他只能拿着咖啡杯走进洗手间。

956
00:33:41.940 --> 00:33:42.160
Yeah.
是啊。

957
00:33:43.200 --> 00:33:46.860
And later, he can't eat in the lunchroom because Pam's sitting in there with Roy.
后来，他没法在休息室吃饭，因为帕姆和罗伊坐在那儿。

958
00:33:47.080 --> 00:33:49.560
This leads to the deleted scene you were talking about.
这就引出了你刚才提到的那个删减片段。

959
00:33:49.720 --> 00:33:50.960
With him eating alone in his car.
他一个人在车里吃饭。

960
00:33:51.100 --> 00:33:51.380
Yeah.
是啊。

961
00:33:51.960 --> 00:33:53.200
Poor Jim, guys.
可怜的吉姆，伙计们。

962
00:33:53.260 --> 00:33:54.080
Poor Jim.
可怜的吉姆。

963
00:33:54.520 --> 00:33:55.360
Poor Jim.
可怜的吉姆。

964
00:33:55.360 --> 00:33:59.700
So then at 11 minutes, 7 seconds, Michael goes back to accounting, and he's like, hey,
然后在11分07秒，迈克尔回到会计部，他说，嘿，

965
00:33:59.800 --> 00:34:00.080
guys.
伙计们。

966
00:34:00.180 --> 00:34:01.700
And I'm really snarky.
我当时说话特别刻薄。

967
00:34:01.820 --> 00:34:04.340
This is like very Angela Martin snarky moment.
这简直是安吉拉·马丁式的刻薄时刻。

968
00:34:04.480 --> 00:34:07.820
I'm like, we haven't finished getting things in order from your last visit.
我说，你上次来的时候留下的烂摊子我们还没收拾完呢。

969
00:34:07.960 --> 00:34:10.180
And he's like, I'm just walking around.
他说，我只是随便走走。

970
00:34:10.180 --> 00:34:11.560
And I go, were you?
我说，是吗？

971
00:34:13.380 --> 00:34:14.720
So ticked off.
气死我了。

972
00:34:14.880 --> 00:34:15.940
You're so mad.
你当时真生气。

973
00:34:16.240 --> 00:34:20.480
Well, this is when Michael gets this big idea to host a sales conteSt.
嗯，这就是迈克尔突发奇想，要举办一场销售竞赛的时候。

974
00:34:20.880 --> 00:34:23.940
Well, listen, because he says we're all there working for the weekend.
听着，因为他说我们都在为了周末而工作。

975
00:34:23.940 --> 00:34:24.760
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

976
00:34:24.760 --> 00:34:26.280
He's working for the week.
他是在为这一周而工作。

977
00:34:26.860 --> 00:34:27.260
What?
什么？

978
00:34:27.520 --> 00:34:28.440
Working for the week.
为这一周而工作。

979
00:34:28.500 --> 00:34:29.600
He's working for the week.
他是在为这一周而工作。

980
00:34:29.640 --> 00:34:31.720
And he wants the sales contest now.
他现在就想搞销售竞赛。

981
00:34:31.880 --> 00:34:38.000
And the prize is a $100 bill until he opens his wallet and he only has $83.
奖金本来是一百美元，结果他打开钱包发现只有八十三美元。

982
00:34:38.580 --> 00:34:42.040
Wait, Jenna, before we get into the sales competition, I do have some journal entries
等等，珍娜，在进入销售竞赛的话题之前，我确实有一些关于这集的

983
00:34:42.040 --> 00:34:42.580
from this.
日记记录。

984
00:34:42.760 --> 00:34:43.380
When do you want them?
你什么时候想听？

985
00:34:43.460 --> 00:34:44.140
Do you want them now?
现在吗？

986
00:34:44.260 --> 00:34:44.460
Now.
现在。

987
00:34:44.680 --> 00:34:45.140
Do you want them late as?
还是晚点？

988
00:34:45.260 --> 00:34:45.940
I say now.
我说现在。

989
00:34:46.100 --> 00:34:46.380
Now?
现在？

990
00:34:46.560 --> 00:34:47.280
Not late as?
不晚点吗？

991
00:34:47.440 --> 00:34:47.680
Okay.
好吧。

992
00:34:48.080 --> 00:34:50.000
Here's my journal entry for the carpet.
这是我关于地毯那集的日记。

993
00:34:50.240 --> 00:34:51.720
I was really excited.
我当时真的很兴奋。

994
00:34:51.720 --> 00:34:54.760
I was like, I wrote this on January 26, 2006.
我写于2006年1月26日。

995
00:34:55.120 --> 00:34:56.620
We got great news.
我们得到了好消息。

996
00:34:56.840 --> 00:34:58.520
We're coming back for season three.
我们要回归拍摄第三季了。

997
00:34:58.820 --> 00:35:01.000
Is this the episode where we found out?
这是我们得知消息的那一集吗？

998
00:35:01.220 --> 00:35:01.640
Yes.
是的。

999
00:35:01.880 --> 00:35:03.180
